This demo redistributes, in modified form, works by others:

- EMA Lightning model weights (ema.pt, decoder.pt) by canberkkkkkk, Apache-2.0.
  https://huggingface.co/canberkkkkkk/ema-lightning
  Modifications: converted to ONNX and split into text, sound and decoder graphs
  (models/*.onnx); models/fp16/sound.onnx is an fp16 conversion of the sound graph.

- normalizer-tr by Erdem Tuna, Apache-2.0, at commit d0bc1bc6523faa4f6257642190bb723b7f4274a5.
  https://github.com/erdemtuna/normalizer-tr
  Modifications: compiled to WebAssembly (models/normalizer.wasm) behind a small C ABI
  (alloc, dealloc, normalize, result_ptr, result_len) using the "fallback" ambiguity policy.
  The binary also contains its Rust dependencies and the Rust standard library; their
  notices are in licenses/normalizer-tr-THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

tts.js reimplements text handling, chunking and the frame timeline of the ema-lightning
Python package (Apache-2.0) in JavaScript.

onnxruntime-web (MIT, Microsoft) is loaded from a CDN at runtime and is not redistributed here.
